      "passage": "[A] The phenomenon of 'green consumerism' emerged into mainstream commerce during the late twentieth century. Environmental awareness transitioned from grassroots ecological activism into consumer purchasing behavior, giving rise to an influential demographic known as 'ethical spenders'.\n\n[B] Extensive consumer research surveys indicate that consumers increasingly evaluate companies on their social record, labor policies, and environmental impact. Among green shoppers, avoiding animal testing is consistently ranked as a paramount consideration—with 48 per cent stating they would refuse to buy products tested on animals. Furthermore, consumers demand transparency, expecting brands to practice authentic honesty and openness regarding supply chains.\n\n[C] However, market analysts identify a pronounced disparity between expressed environmental concern and actual purchasing behavior. While up to 90 per cent of survey respondents state they care about environmental protection, a substantial proportion are classified as 'armchair ethicals'—individuals who express sympathy for green causes but whose actual retail transactions remain dominated by price and convenience.\n\n[A] Stories read in early childhood exert a profound, lasting influence on emotional intelligence, moral imagination, and linguistic fluency.\n\n[B] Psychologists emphasize that fairy tales and allegorical narratives allow young children to process complex psychological fears—such as abandonment, sibling rivalry, and personal inadequacy—within a safe, symbolic aesthetic framework.\n\n[C] Furthermore, shared bedtime reading fosters deep familial attachment and expands receptive vocabulary far beyond everyday conversational vernacular.\n\n[A] The evolution of architectural glass from simple blown window panes into high-performance structural building envelopes has redefined urban skylines across the globe.\n\n[B] Modern double- and triple-glazed curtain walls incorporate low-emissivity (low-E) metallic coatings and inert argon gas fills. These coatings reflect infrared thermal radiation while allowing visible spectrum daylight to penetrate, drastically reducing building heating and cooling energy loads.\n\n[C] Furthermore, laminated and toughened structural glass now carries immense load-bearing weights, allowing architects to construct breathtaking transparent canopies, spiral staircases, and column-free atrium facades.",
