      "minWords": 150,
      "level": "Band 7.0 - 8.5",
      "prompt": "The pie chart illustrates comparative data concerning key indices in society, urbanization & demographics across four industrialized economies (Country A, Country B, Country C, and Country D) between 2000 and 2024.\nSummarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.\nWrite at least 150 words.",
      "sampleAnswerBand8": "The provided pie chart details comparative statistics regarding foundational metrics in society, urbanization & demographics across four developed countries—namely Country A, Country B, Country C, and Country D—spanning a 24-year timeframe from 2000 to 2024.\n\nOverall, it is readily apparent from the data that all four economies recorded an upward trajectory over the observed period. Furthermore, while Country A consistently maintained the highest overall figures throughout, Country D exhibited the most dramatic rate of expansion, successfully overtaking Country C in the latter half of the timeframe.\n\nIn 2000, Country A spearheaded the ranking with approximately 46%, followed closely by Country B at 38%. Over the following twelve years, Country A witnessed a steady climb, reaching 58% in 2012 before peaking at a study-high of 68% in the final year. In marked contrast, figures for Country B experienced moderate oscillations between 35% and 42%, ultimately stabilizing at 44% by 2024.\n\nTurning to the remaining nations, Country C and Country D commenced the period at modest levels of 22% and 14% respectively. However, Country D demonstrated a pronounced acceleration after 2010, nearly tripling its initial percentage to finish at 39%. This surge enabled Country D to surpass Country C, which registered only marginal growth to conclude at 31%.",
      "outlineBreakdown": {
        "intro": "Paraphrase lại đề bài: biểu đồ miêu tả các chỉ số trong lĩnh vực tương ứng tại 4 quốc gia giai đoạn 2000 - 2024.",
        "overview": "Nêu 2 đặc điểm nổi bật nhất: cả 4 nước đều có xu hướng tăng; Country A luôn dẫn đầu và Country D tăng trưởng mạnh nhất.",
        "body1": "Phân tích nhóm số liệu dẫn đầu (Country A và B) với mốc xuất phát, điểm biến động và mốc về đích.",
        "body2": "Phân tích nhóm số liệu thấp hơn (Country C và D) cùng điểm bứt phá vượt mặt (overtaking) sau năm 2010 của Country D."
      },
