      "id": "spe_test_54",
      "skill": "speaking",
      "testNum": 54,
      "title": "Speaking Part 3 (Test 54): Analytical Discourse on Economy, Business & Globalization",
      "part": "Part 3",
      "topic": "economy",
      "topicName": "Economy, Business & Globalization",
      "level": "Band 7.0 - 8.5",
      "prompts": [
        "1. What role should governmental legislation play in regulating developments in economy, business & globalization?",
        "2. Some commentators argue that international accords are ineffective in this field. Do you agree?",
        "3. How do generational differences influence how older and younger citizens perceive economy, business & globalization?",
        "4. In what ways might artificial intelligence reshape this field over the upcoming two decades?"
      ],
      "modelResponseBand8": "1. From my perspective, statutory legislation acts as an extraordinarily potent behavioral catalyst. While ethical appeals frequently fall on deaf ears, statutory fines and fiscal incentives compel organizations to implement responsible practices with remarkable speed.\n\n2. I would respectfully disagree with that assertion. Although enforcement mechanisms can admittedly be challenging across sovereign boundaries, multilateral accords establish standardized global benchmarks without which coordinated action against transnational crises would be utterly impossible.\n\n3. There is undeniably a generational divergence. Senior demographics frequently approach these issues with conservative caution, prioritizing stability and risk aversion. In stark contrast, younger generations tend to be significantly more receptive to disruptive change and vocal in demanding progressive overhauls.\n\n4. Speculating on the foreseeable future, I envision artificial intelligence acting as a major accelerator. We will likely witness automated analytical frameworks that optimize operational logistics and eliminate routine inefficiencies, allowing human specialists to focus on high-level strategic governance.",
      "outlineStrategy": "Tư duy vĩ mô: Áp dụng 'On the one hand... On the other hand', phân tích tác động chính sách (Socio-economic impact) và suy đoán tương lai (Speculation).",
